  public record Money(BigDecimal amount, Currency currency) {
     // compact constructor — validation at the ONLY entry point
     public Money {
        if (amount.signum() < 0) throw new IllegalArgumentException();
        Objects.requireNonNull(currency);
     }
     public Money add(Money o) {          // returns NEW instance
        return new Money(amount.add(o.amount), currency);
     }
  }

  record TransferRequest(String from, String to, Money amount) {}
  record TransferCompleted(String txnId, Money amount, Instant at) {}

  Generated for free:  equals()  hashCode()  toString()  accessors()
  Fields are private + final → true Encapsulation & Immutability.

  SOLID: SRP — a record only carries data, no behavior creep.
  Pattern: Value Object (DDD). Thread-safe by immutability.
  Call chain: controller(TransferRequest) → service → new Money() → event.
```
